# Mary Had a Little Lamb (repertoire plan: mary-had-a-little-lamb). The familiar tune on strings
# 3 and 2 in first position: the open string 3 (G), string 3 fret 2 (A) with finger 2, the open
# string 2 (B) and string 2 fret 3 (D) with finger 3. The teacher strums G throughout, with D7
# under bars 3 and 7.
title: Mary Had a Little Lamb
id: mary-had-a-little-lamb
composer: Lowell Mason (tune, adapted); words by Sarah Josepha Hale
source: Poem published in 1830, sung to Lowell Mason's tune from the 1830s; arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (tune and words); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 1
tags: melody, two strings, lyrics, beginner
tempo: 96
time: 4/4
key: G

track: Melody
role: lead
